  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x78E2" flags="0x0">
    <title>4C 2 C6 TPS 20 Look Up Table -&gt;4C730 in OneLambda</title>
    <description>TPS is processed by tables at 4c708 and 4c730 in a similar way but there are a couple of offsets added before the ADC value lookup (one must be the &quot;reset TPS&quot; offset, but not sure about the other) and then there is a myriad of processing after the TPS degrees value is looked up before it becomes our recognised TPS value. The strange table at 4c762 is involved in this along with a dozen or so other values...&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;The 5AM uses a linear approximation between 20 points - firstly to convert the adc value to a notional position in 20 steps (table 4c708) and then to convert this position to a degree value (table 4c730).</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="4" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
